{"id":"word:hebrew:H6963","type":"word","title":"קוֹל","subtitle":"H6963 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"a voice or sound","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to קוֹל (H6963) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 506 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"קוֹל (qôwl) means a voice or sound First listed occurrence: 1Chr 14 15."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"קוֹל","transliteration":"qôwl","pronunciation":"kole","strong":"H6963","lemmaId":"hebrew:H6963","partOfSpeech":"n-m","forms":["ק֣וֹל","בְּ/ק֣וֹל","ק֥וֹל","ק֤וֹל","וְ/ק֣וֹל"],"morphs":[["HNcmsc",118],["HR/Ncmsc",111],["HNcmsa",47],["HC/Ncmsc",28],["HNcmsc/Sp3ms",23],["HNcmsc/Sp1cs",23],["HR/Ncmsc/Sp1cs",22],["HR/Ncmsa",18],["HNcmsc/Sp3mp",17],["HR/Ncmsc/Sp3ms",15]]},"definitions":{"short":"a voice or sound","usage":"aloud, bleating, crackling, cry ( out), fame, lightness, lowing, noise, hold peace, (pro-) claim, proclamation, sing, sound, spark, thunder(-ing), voice, yell.","full":"H6963. qol קוֺל (sometimes, with prefix and suffix, קֹל ) 506 noun masculine Gen 39:14 sound, voice ; — absolute קוֺל 4:10 + ( הַקֹּל 27:22 ; 45:16 ); construct קוֺל 3:8 + ( וְקֹל Exod 19:16 , לְקֹל 4:8 (twice in verse)); suffix קוֺלִי 1Sam 26:17 +, קוֺלְךָ Judg 18:25 +, etc. ( קֹלִי Gen 22:18 , קֹלֶ֑ךָ Exod 3:18 , etc.); plural (usually of thunder) קֹלֹת 9:23 4 t., קוֺלֹת 20:18 (Gi 20:15 ), קֹלוֺת 1Sam 2:17 5 t.; — 1 sound: especially a. of human voice Josh 6:10 ; 2Kin 7:10 ; in speech Gen 27:22 (twice in verse); 1Sam 1:13 ; 24:17 ; 26:17 (twice in verse); recognized ( הִכִּיר ) 26:17 ; Jer 18:3 ; ק ׳יְפֵה Ezek 33:32 pleasant of voice , compare Song 2:14 (twice in verse); 8:13 ; in singing Exod 32:18 ; 2Sam 19:36 ; Isa 52:8 , calling Judg 9:7 , shouting Exod 32:17 ; 1Sam 4:6 (twice in verse); 1Kin 1:40 ; Ezra 3:13 , rejoicing Jer 7:34 (4 t. in verse) = 16:9 ; 25:10 ; 33:11 , praise Psa 66:8 ; 26:7 ; Joel 2:10 , laughter Jer 30:19 , weeping Gen 21:16 ; Judg 2:4 ; 1Sam 11:4 ; Ruth 1:9 , 14 ; Ezra 3:13 , outcry Gen 39:15 , 18 ; 1Sam 4:14 ; Jer 8:19 , distress, lament 9:18 ; Ezek 27:30 ; Zech 11:3 ; Psa 102:6 , supplication 28:2 ; 28:6 ; 31:23 ; 86:6 ; adverb ׳ק אֶחָד with one voice Exod 24:3 ; 2Chr 5:13 , ׳ק גָּדוֺל loud voice 2Sam 15:23 + (compare ׳בְּק ׳ג Gen 39:14 ; 1Sam 28:12 +), ׳ק רָם Deut 27:14 ; ק ׳נָשָׂא Gen 21:16 + (see נָשָׂא 1b (5)), ק ׳הֵרִים 39:15 + (see דום Hiph`il ); on ׳ק as independent noun, followed by subject + verb of calling Psa 3:5 ; 27:7 ; 142:2 see Ges § 144m b. of ׳י Gen 3:8 , 10 ; Isa 6:8 ; Exod 19:19 ; 1Kin 19:3 ; Micah 6:9 ; Ezek 10:5 (compare also 2b ) +; adverb ׳ק גָּדוֺל Deut 5:19 ; Ezek 9:1 ; ׳ק דַקָּה דְּמָמָה 1Kin 19:12 . c. of seraph Isa 6:4 . d. of angel Dan 8:16 ( ׳ק אָדָם i.e. in human speech, compare Bev); ׳ק דְּבָרָיו 10:6 , 9 (twice in verse). e. of animals: bleating of sheep 1Sam 15:14 , lowing of cattle 15:14 ; Jer 9:9 , neighing of horses 8:16 , roaring of lion Amos 3:4 ; Jer 2:15 +, hissing of serpent 46:22 (in simile), singing of birds Nahum 2:8 ; Zeph 2:14 ; Psa 104:12 ; Song 2:12 ; Eccl 12:4 . f. exclamation, at beginning of clause , a sound of...! = hark! Gen 4:10 ; Isa 13:4 ; 40:3 ; 52:8 ; Jer 4:15 ; 10:22 ; 50:28 ; Song 2:8 ; 5:2 (Ges § 146b ). 2 sound: a. of instrument, especially ׳ק (הַ)שֹּׁפָר Exod 9:16 ; 20:18 (Gi 20:15 ) Amos 2:2 ; 1Kin 1:41 +, וגו ׳חֲצֹצְרוֺת 2Chr 5:13 , כִּנּוֺר Ezek 26:13 , עוּנָב Job 21:12 ; of מַּעֲמֹנִים on high priest's robe Exod 28:35 . b. thunder-clap or peal (compare Dr 1Sam 12:17 ), י ׳קוֺל (or קוֺלוֺ ) Amos 1:2 ; Isa 30:30-31 , Jer 10:13 = 51:16 , Joel 2:11 ; Joel 4:16; Psa 18:14 = 2Sam 22:14 ; Psa 29:3 ; 29:7 ; 46:7 ; Job 37:4 (compare 1Sam 7:10 ; Psa 77:18 ; 77:19 ; 104:7 ), so especially plural absolute (see above) Exod 9:23 , 28 , 29 , 33 , 34 ; 19:16 ; 20:18 (Gi 20:15 ), 1Sam 7:10 ; 12:17-18 , Job 28:26 = 38:25 . c. רַגְלֶיהָ קוֺל 1Kin 14:6 compare 2Kin 6:32 , and (probably) Gen 3:8 ; also ׳ק (הַ)צְּעָדָה 2Sam 5:24 = 1Chr 14:15 ; of runners 2Kin 11:13 ; 2Chr 23:12 . d. stamping of hoofs Jer 47:3 ; Ezek 26:10 ( +chariots, etc.), compare 1Kin 1:41 . e. of chariots Nahum 3:2 ; Joel 2:5 ; wheels Ezek 3:13 ; whip Nahum 3:2 . f. of sea, and great waters Hab 3:10 ; Ezek 1:24 ; 43:2 ; Psa 93:3 ; 93:4 , compare Jer 50:42 (in simile); ׳ק צִנּוֺרֶיךָ Psa 42:8 . g. earthquake Ezek 37:7 . h. a fall Jer 49:21 ; Ezek 26:15 ; 31:16 . i. of a multitude 1Sam 4:14 ; Isa 13:4 ; Ezek 23:42 . j. din of war Exod 32:17 ; Jer 50:22 , 46 ; 51:55 ; Lam 2:7 . k. of wings Ezek 1:24 ; 3:13 ; 10:5 . l. flame Joel 2:5 ; crackling of thorns Eccl 7:6 ; rustling of leaves Lev 26:36 . m. millstones Jer 25:10 ; Eccl 12:4 . 3 of articulate speech, thing said: a. (1) often of human advice, command, entreaty Gen 3:17 ; 4:23 ; Exod 3:18 ; 4:1 , 9 ; Deut 1:45 ; 21:18 (twice in verse); 21:20 ; 1Sam 2:25 ; 8:7 , 9 ; 2Sam 12:18 ; ׳ק דִּבְרֵיכֶם Deut 1:34 ; 5:25 ; even of written words 2Kin 10:6 ; so also ׳ק הָאֹת Exod 4:8 (twice in verse) voice (teaching) of the sign . (2) of a report Gen 45:16 ; Eccl 10:20 . (3) of a proclamation Exod 36:6 (P), 2Chr 24:9 ; 30:5 ; 36:22 = Ezra 1:1 ; 10:7 ; Neh 8:15 . (4) ׳ק אָלָה Lev 5:1 utterance of adjuration. b. often (especially Deuteronomy, Jeremiah) of words of ׳י Gen 22:18 ; 26:5 ; Exod 5:2 ; 15:26 ; 19:5 ; Deut 8:20 ; 9:23 ; 13:15 ; Deuteronomy 13:19 +, Judg 2:2 , 20 ; 6:10 ; 1Sam 12:14-15 , 15:1 , 19 , 20 , 22 ; Jer 3:13 , 25 ; 7:23 +; of י ׳מַלְאַךְ Exod 23:21-22 ,. &#8212; קֹל Jer 3:9 see below קלל . קֹל noun [masculine] lightness, frivolity (so Vrss Ki Gie; Gf thinks = קָלוֺן ; &gt; = voice ); — זְנוּנָהּ מִקֹּל Jer 3:9 . &#8212; קֹל voice , see קוֺל . קול (√ of following; Biblical Hebrew קוֺל קול, ).","rootNote":"or קֹל ; from an unused root meaning to call aloud;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 14 15","keyReferences":["1Chr 14 15","1Chr 15 16","1C